sentences.l:
“Thanks to God who of-the world is lord!
Before I-was in-want, now rich I-am,
for I-have wealth and land and gold and estate,
and are my sons-in-law Infantes of Carrión;

sentences.t:
Grandes son los gozos en Valençia [la mayor]
de todas sus conpañas [de] mio Çid el Canpeador,
d' aquesta arrancada que lidiaron de coraçón;

sentences.l:
Great are the joys in Valençia [the great]
of all his companies [of] my Çid the Campeador,
from this rout that they-fought with heart;

sentences.t:
grandes son los gozos de s[o]s yernos amos a dos:
valía de çinco mill marcos ganaron amos a dos;
muchos tienen por ricos ifantes de Carrión.

sentences.l:
great are the joys of h[i]s sons-in-law both two:
value of five thousand marks they-won both two;
many hold as rich Infantes of Carrión.

sentences.t:
Ellos con los otros vinieron a la cort;
aquí está con mio Çid el obispo do Jero[me],
el bueno de Álbar Fáñez cavallero lidiador,
e otros muchos que crió el Campeador;

sentences.l:
They with the others came to the court;
here is with my Çid the bishop don Jero[me],
the good of Albar Fáñez knight fighting,
and others many whom brought-up the Campeador;

sentences.t:
quando entraron ifantes de Carrión,
recibiólos Minaya por mio Çid el Campeador;
“Acá, venid, cuñados, que mas valemos por vos.”

sentences.l:
when entered Infantes of Carrión,
received-them Minaya for my Çid the Campeador;
“Hither, come, kinsmen, for more we-are-worth through you.”

sentences.t:
A estas palabras fabló [ifant] Ferran[do]:
“Grado al Criador e a vos, Çid ondrado,
tantos avemos de averes que no son contados;

sentences.l:
At these words spoke [Infante] Ferran[do]:
“Thanks to-the Creator and to you, Çid honoured,
so-much we-have of goods that not they-are counted;

sentences.t:
Vassallos de mio Çid se[d]iense sonrrisando:
quien lidiara mejor o quien f[o]ra en alcanço;
mas non fallavan i a Dí[da]go ni a Ferrando.

sentences.l:
Vassals of my Çid were-sitting smiling:
who had-fought better or who had-g[o]ne in pursuit;
but not they-found there Dí[da]go nor Ferrando.
